---
const durable = [
  { name: "Contracts", body: "What each component promises: inputs, outputs, side effects and invariants. People own these." },
  { name: "Evidence", body: "Tests, traces and benchmarks showing the promises hold. Machines produce it and re-run it constantly." },
  { name: "The map", body: "How components relate: who calls whom, what data flows where, who owns what. Derived from code." },
];
---

<section class="section thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="thesis-title">The idea</h2>
    <p class="display-m statement">
      Changes should be understood as shifts in meaning, scored by risk, and approved by evidence rather
      than by someone reading lines.
    </p>
    <div class="durable">
      <p class="body-l muted intro">
        Users never see code. They see behavior. So the source of truth moves to three things that outlive
        any version of the code, and agents can rewrite the rest freely.
      </p>
      <dl class="list">
        {
          durable.map((d) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="title">{d.name}</dt>
              <dd class="muted">{d.body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .statement {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .durable {
    margin-top: clamp(var(--space-8), 3rem + 4vw, var(--space-10));
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .durable {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
      gap: var(--space-9);
    }
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 30rem;
  }

  .list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 13rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .list > div {
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  dd {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
